-- Q5874: Data Protection Technologies [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per NIST SP 800-57 Part 1 Section 7.2, a deactivated key has passed its cryptoperiod and is no longer used for applying cryptographic protection (encryption) but may still be used for processing previously protected data (decryption). The key retains decrypt-only capability.
Wrong (A): An active key is within its cryptoperiod and authorized for both encryption and decryption. This key has passed its expiration date and can no longer encrypt.
Wrong (C): A suspended key is temporarily taken out of normal use due to a suspected compromise and may be reactivated. This key was permanently transitioned, not temporarily paused.
Wrong (D): A destroyed key has been irreversibly deleted and cannot perform any cryptographic operations, including decryption of existing records.$EXPL$
