  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per NIST SP 800-111, full disk encryption protects data at rest by encrypting the entire contents of a storage device. If a laptop is lost or stolen, FDE renders stored data unreadable to anyone without the authentication credentials or decryption key.
